From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ARMDeck <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: samsung-amb655uv01: run the 90 Hz DSI link at the
 OnePlus rate

The panel runs in DSI command mode with DSC (8 bits per pixel, 8 bits per
component, two 540x48 slices per line) over 4 lanes. The msm DSI host has
no fixed link rate for command mode: it derives the pixel, byte and bit
clocks from the mode (dsi_get_pclk_rate(),
dsi_adjust_pclk_for_compression(), dsi_byte_clk_get_rate(),
msm_dsi_host_get_phy_clk_req()):

  pclk = clock * (htotal - hdisplay + hdisplay * 8 / 24) / htotal
  byte = pclk * 24 / (8 * 4)
  bit  = byte * 8                                    (per lane)

With clock = htotal * vtotal * 90 / 1000 kHz this reduces to
bit = 6 * vtotal * 90 * (htotal - 720), about 1.3 Mbps per unit of htotal.

The current 90 Hz mode (htotal 1120, vtotal 2414, 243331 kHz) gives a
pixel clock of 86.90 MHz and 521.4 Mbps per lane. The DPU sends 360 pixel
clocks per compressed line, so one frame (2400 lines) takes 9.9 ms of the
11.1 ms refresh period.

The OnePlus vendor device tree for this panel
(dsi-panel-oplus19101samsung-amb655uv01-1080-2400-90fps.dtsi) sets
qcom,mdss-dsi-panel-clockrate = <652800000> in both its 60 Hz and its
90 Hz timing, with the same porches as this driver (8/24/8). The vendor
DSI driver uses that value as the per-lane bit clock
(dsi_ctrl_update_link_freqs(): bit_rate = clk_rate_hz * lanes,
pclk = bit_rate / 24), so the stock firmware runs a 108.8 MHz pixel clock
and moves a 90 Hz frame in about 8.0 ms.

Widen the horizontal back porch of the 90 Hz mode from 8 to 108
(htotal 1220, clock 265057 kHz):

  pclk 108629918 Hz, byte 81472438 Hz, bit 651779504 bps per lane

htotal 1220 is the largest value that stays at or below the vendor's
652.8 Mbps (htotal 1221 would give 653.08 Mbps). A frame now takes about
7.95 ms, as on the stock firmware.

Nothing else changes:

- The porches are never sent to a command-mode panel. In command mode
  dsi_timing_setup() only programs DSI_CMD_MDP_STREAM0_TOTAL (compressed
  line width and vdisplay), and the DPU interface timing engine is used
  for video mode only. The front porch (8) and the sync width (24) keep
  the vendor values; the extra 100 pixels go to the back porch.
- vtotal and the refresh rate are unchanged (drm_mode_vrefresh() returns
  90 for the old and the new mode), so the tear check setup (vsync_count,
  sync height, start position), the DPU line time (4603 ns) and the DPU
  core clock and bandwidth votes, which are computed from vtotal,
  hdisplay and the refresh rate, stay the same.
- The DSC configuration (slice size, bits per pixel) is set at probe and
  the picture size comes from hdisplay and vdisplay; none of it depends
  on htotal.
- The 7nm PHY PLL reaches 651.78 MHz with no output divider. The VCO
  range of this PHY revision (v4.1) is 600 MHz to 5 GHz in both the
  mainline and the vendor PLL drivers, so the vendor's 652.8 MHz is
  reached the same way. The D-PHY timings mainline computes for this
  rate (00 17 06 07 21 20 06 06 04 02 04 00 16 16) are close to the
  vendor table for 652.8 Mbps (00 1a 06 06 22 20 07 06 04 02 04 00 16 16).
- The byte clock (81.5 MHz) stays below the lowest DSI OPP (187.5 MHz),
  so the voltage vote does not change.

The 60 Hz mode is left as it is: the power-on sequence always sets the
panel itself to 90 Hz (DCS 0x60 0x10), and a working 60 Hz mode is a
separate change.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655uv01.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655uv01.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655uv01.c
index 265e023..1e82acb 100755
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655uv01.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655uv01.c
@@ -180,11 +180,18 @@ static int samsung_amb655uv01_unprepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 
 static const struct drm_display_mode samsung_amb655uv01_modes[] = {
 	{ /* 90Hz Mode */
-		.clock = (1080 + 8 + 24 + 8) * (2400 + 4 + 4 + 6) * 90 / 1000,
+		/*
+		 * Command mode: the porches are not sent to the panel, but msm
+		 * DSI derives the link rate from this mode. The 108-pixel back
+		 * porch gives 651.78 Mbps per lane, just below the 652.8 Mbps
+		 * OnePlus uses (qcom,mdss-dsi-panel-clockrate). With the
+		 * vendor porches (htotal 1120) the link ran at 521 Mbps.
+		 */
+		.clock = (1080 + 8 + 24 + 108) * (2400 + 4 + 4 + 6) * 90 / 1000,
 		.hdisplay = 1080,
 		.hsync_start = 1080 + 8,
 		.hsync_end = 1080 + 8 + 24,
-		.htotal = 1080 + 8 + 24 + 8,
+		.htotal = 1080 + 8 + 24 + 108,
 		.vdisplay = 2400,
 		.vsync_start = 2400 + 4,
 		.vsync_end = 2400 + 4 + 4,
-- 
